{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Introduce new rules for B2B sales of telecommunication contracts",
        "additional_details": "We call for Regulatory Changes to protect the UK small business economy from predatory telecom practices, through the following legislative and regulatory actions: \r\nPre-Contract Disclosure Requirements: Mandate that no B2B verbal contract is legally binding until the business owner has received, reviewed, and signed a clear written summary of all costs and terms after the initial phone call.\r\nIntroduce Mandatory 14-Day Cooling-Off Period\r\nReview Mis-selling Practices and Enforcement",
        "background": "We call on the UK Government to introduce an immediate, mandatory 14-day cooling-off period for all business telecommunications contracts sold over the phone. Furthermore, we demand a review of the regulatory oversight and enforcement against predatory sales tactics.",
